I’ll inspect the diffraction data and metadata first, then use the available indexing/search and GSAS-II tooling to build and refine the smallest defensible multiphase model. I’ll keep phase identification and quantitative uncertainty separate so weakly constrained fractions are not overstated.

The chemistry narrows the plausible crystalline products to copper tungstates plus possible residual CuO/WO₃, but I’m treating that only as a prior. I’m now matching all relevant COD structures against the measured peak positions and checking whether any residual peaks demand an additional phase.

The peak lattice is internally consistent with ambient triclinic CuWO₄ (P‑1): the characteristic low-angle lines and the dense high-angle splitting are all accounted for. The nearest database entry is a high-pressure CuWO₄ determination, so I’m using its atom topology only and replacing/refining the cell against this ambient-pressure pattern; I will not treat its published high-pressure cell as the answer.

The one-phase whole-pattern model already reaches an 8.0% weighted profile residual and leaves no unmatched Bragg family; remaining misfit is concentrated at the strongest CuWO₄ peaks. I’m testing whether that comes from the borrowed high-pressure atom coordinates, specimen texture, or an over-flexible peak-width function before locking the final project.

A scale-only impurity screen rules out residual CuO and gives no meaningful support for Cu₃WO₆, but a small WO₃ contribution lowers Rwp from 7.65% to 7.34% with a positive scale. I’m comparing the known WO₃ polymorphs now; because its strongest lines overlap CuWO₄, the exact minor-phase fraction needs a stricter model-selection check.

The final model is two-phase: triclinic CuWO₄ plus a small monoclinic WO₃ remainder. Across the WO₃ polymorph screen, the room-temperature monoclinic model is clearly preferred; after joint refinement it gives about 97.9/2.1 wt% and Rwp ≈ 7.17%. I’m now exporting the converged project, phase CIFs, profile, and uncertainty notes from that exact refinement state.

Identified crystalline phases:

- Triclinic CuWO₄, P-1: **97.91 wt%**
- Monoclinic WO₃, P2₁/c: **2.09 wt%**

Fractions are normalized over modeled crystalline phases. Final fit: Rwp 7.166%, Rp 5.217%, GOF 2.953. The WO₃ systematic uncertainty is approximately ±0.5 wt%; amorphous content is not quantified.

